  "input_contract": {
    "request": "HPRDQ001 96-byte header; cmd1 acquire, cmd2 exact outstanding resume, cmd3 release held loan and finish",
    "result": "HBRDS001 kind6 grants the actual owned parent FD and basename bytes without reopening, duplicating or transferring ownership; kind0 final completion is an empty payload; kind3 original structured error",
    "close": "Trusted parent_directory_close(context) constructs cmd3 from the recorded sequence; external inputs cannot choose an FD to close",
    "lifetime": "Exactly one held loan per context. The parent context remains the sole owner while synchronous child operations borrow its numeric descriptor. Acquire, release, destruction and arbitrary resume refuse during the held state.",
    "after_close": "All remaining cleanup follows original HIA policy; terminal response stays borrowed until release. Destroy requires an idle released context.",
    "final_basename": "Final target need not exist and is not opened during parent acquisition. Final embedded NUL is preserved as basename data, matching original parent(); later file open must reject it.",
    "ownership_ledger": "The native boundary records every actual opened descriptor, only closes owned entries, exposes no caller-selected OS effect and supports descriptor zero. EOF closes each held parent via the HIA close transition."
  },
